The problem is that until you have received at least one gift,
unaligned artifacts like Frost Brand are not eligible to be created as
a gift.  The only chaotic artifacts are:

Grimtooth    
Orcrist      
Sting        
Stormbringer 
The Longbow of Diana      
The Master Key of Thievery

The last two are quest artifacts, and Grimtooth is not eligible to be
given as a gift to an elf.  So if Orcrist, Sting, and Stormbringer
already exist in your game, and you've received no gifts, then you
will never recieve another artifact via sacrificing.

mk_artifact() iterates through the entire artifact list and builds a
list of which ones are eligible to be created.  The relevant condition
related to alignment and gifts (which must be true to add the artifact
to the list) is:

a->alignment == alignment || (a->alignment == A_NONE && u.ugifts > 0)

"alignment" is the alignment of the altar, a->alignment is the
alignment of the artifact, and u.ugifts is the number of gifts the
player has already received.  So if u.ugifts is zero, then only
coaligned artifacts are eligible for creation.  If all of the
coaligned artifacts are ineligible for other reasons, then artifact
creation will fail, and mk_artifact will return null.

This one is already on the fixed bug list:

C343-358 	Fixed 	If no co-aligned artifacts are available for gifting
                  when required, gifting fails repeatedly.


